# The wire fixtures are BYTES, and the whole point of them is that they stay
# byte-exact across every machine that checks this repository out. Git's own
# heuristic already treats them as binary - the 4-byte big-endian header length
# starts with NULs - but relying on a heuristic to protect the thing that exists
# to stop silent drift is the wrong shape. Say it outright.
#
# Written on a repository whose maintainer works on Windows, where a checkout
# with core.autocrlf=true is the default path to a corrupted fixture.
web/src/transport/__fixtures__/requests/*.bin binary

# ONNX graphs and model weights, for the same reason. artifacts/ is gitignored
# today, but a rule that only works because the file is absent is not a rule.
*.onnx binary
*.pt binary

# Shell scripts run on Linux - in a container, or on Cloud Build. A CRLF
# shebang line is reported as "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M", which is a
# genuinely baffling error the first time somebody meets it.
*.sh text eol=lf
service/Dockerfile text eol=lf
